cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hermes-jailbench, please cite it as below."
title: "hermes-jailbench: a jailbreak regression benchmark for LLM endpoints"
abstract: >-
  hermes-jailbench is a jailbreak regression benchmark that runs a repeatable
  battery of known-pattern attacks against an LLM endpoint and returns
  deterministic refusal/partial/compliance scores, so teams can detect when a
  model or prompt change silently weakens established refusals. It uses a
  zero-LLM keyword scorer, supports a no-key dry-run and demo, and is a
  regression baseline for known patterns rather than a novel-attack red-team.
type: software
authors:
